 ## Overview
-NeRF-RPN is a method for 3D object detection and instance segmentation that utilizes a multi-scale Object-NeRF architecture to predict 3D bounding boxes and class labels directly from a neural radiance field [S1]. It distinguishes itself from standard NeRF variants by enabling the regression of object locations without requiring rendered views for the detection step, and it supports the detection of unlabeled objects as a general framework [S1].
+NeRF-RPN is a 3D object detection framework that utilizes a multi-scale Object-NeRF architecture to regress 3D axis-aligned bounding boxes (AABB) and classify objects directly from a neural radiance field [S1]. It distinguishes itself from standard NeRF variants by enabling 3D localization without rendering intermediate views, serving as a general framework capable of detecting objects even without class labels [S1].
 
